{"title":"Analytic Geometry","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In mathematics,  analytic geometry, also known as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coordinate_geometry\" title=\"Coordinate geometry\">coordinate geometry</a> or Cartesian geometry, is the study of geometry using a coordinate plane. More generally, analytical geometry deals with finding the coordinates and slopes of certain shapes to find results. This contrasts with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Synthetic_geometry\" title=\"Synthetic geometry\">synthetic geometry</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Analytic_Geometry&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018072842\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 7/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.382      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.382      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16177:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018072842 and revision id 285471. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}